WEBVTT

00:45.003 --> 00:47.965
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

00:48.757 --> 00:52.344
EPISODE 6

00:57.558 --> 00:58.850
82.

01:02.312 --> 01:03.313
80.

01:03.981 --> 01:04.982
- 81.
- 81.

01:05.732 --> 01:06.733
82.

01:07.067 --> 01:08.610
- One more.
- 83.

01:08.694 --> 01:10.070
- 84.
- 84.

01:10.654 --> 01:12.531
- 85.
- Good.

01:12.614 --> 01:14.408
- 86.
- Just 4 more.

01:14.491 --> 01:15.492
- 87.
- Stop.

01:17.452 --> 01:18.453
Why are you working so hard?

01:18.537 --> 01:19.621
Did something happen on leave?

01:20.080 --> 01:21.081
No, sir.

01:22.624 --> 01:24.835
After working at that
famous tteokbokki place

01:27.671 --> 01:28.672
I realized that...

01:29.548 --> 01:30.882
if I don't have the stamina for it

01:31.508 --> 01:32.884
I won't be able to run a business, sir.

01:33.302 --> 01:34.761
You worked during your leave?

01:35.137 --> 01:36.555
I knew you were crazy

01:36.638 --> 01:37.764
but I didn't realize you were this crazy.

01:39.016 --> 01:42.144
I thought it might help my mom
with her restaurant, sir.

01:42.436 --> 01:43.604
Hey...

01:43.687 --> 01:45.105
I get where you're coming from...

01:45.188 --> 01:46.690
but you're a little too enthusiastic.

01:49.359 --> 01:51.445
So, in this upcoming training

01:51.528 --> 01:52.779
I want to try really hard too.

01:53.113 --> 01:54.740
I heard it's tough

01:54.948 --> 01:56.825
but doesn't that mean I can level up?

01:57.075 --> 01:59.077
This guy's completely
lost touch with reality.

01:59.286 --> 02:00.954
You've never heard of the Viper Unit?

02:01.038 --> 02:02.289
The legendary Viper Unit

02:02.372 --> 02:04.374
that the best units couldn't touch.

02:06.209 --> 02:07.502
The Viper Unit...

02:08.003 --> 02:09.296
Are they really that amazing?

02:09.379 --> 02:10.922
All right, let's switch
people and continue.

02:11.256 --> 02:12.257
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

02:15.552 --> 02:16.553
Ready.

02:16.637 --> 02:18.430
Even their name is brutal.

02:18.513 --> 02:19.806
Begin.

02:20.641 --> 02:21.725
The Viper Unit

02:22.059 --> 02:23.477
is full of venom.

02:23.602 --> 02:25.979
Their mindset is different from ours.

02:26.063 --> 02:28.607
They go full method actor.

02:29.066 --> 02:30.484
"We are not an opposing force."

02:30.567 --> 02:33.362
"We train as if we were
real North Korean soldiers."

02:33.445 --> 02:35.113
"Body, heart, and spirit."

02:35.197 --> 02:36.865
"We must engage with all our hearts"

02:36.948 --> 02:39.076
"to fight strong enemies"

02:39.159 --> 02:41.411
"and build our resolve, got it?"

02:41.745 --> 02:43.997
The moment they say that,
from their tone and actions

02:44.081 --> 02:46.416
they start acting exactly
like soldiers from the North.

02:46.500 --> 02:48.460
"Comrade Choi, confirmed location."

02:48.543 --> 02:49.711
"Move it!" They will say.

02:49.795 --> 02:52.589
Then they fly through the mountains
like it's their own front yard.

02:52.673 --> 02:55.676
"We will annihilate
every last one. Understood?"

02:55.759 --> 02:56.760
"Understood!"

02:56.843 --> 02:58.553
The moment you show an opening

02:58.679 --> 03:00.263
they'll open their jaws

03:00.347 --> 03:02.140
and shove a poison fang into your vitals.

03:02.599 --> 03:04.434
And very slowly...

03:04.893 --> 03:06.937
they wait for their opponent to die.

03:07.020 --> 03:08.021
Like a viper

03:08.105 --> 03:09.356
as their name suggests.

03:11.066 --> 03:14.569
Killed.

03:19.700 --> 03:20.784
"Squad wiped out!"

03:20.867 --> 03:22.953
"Viper Unit's mission is complete!"

03:25.497 --> 03:27.499
What's the point of all this
physical training?

03:27.624 --> 03:29.126
Compared to those brutal guys

03:29.209 --> 03:30.711
we're just a bunch of punks.

03:30.794 --> 03:32.254
Private First Class Tak Mun-ik.

03:33.130 --> 03:34.798
What? Scared already?

03:36.049 --> 03:37.551
You didn't even do one, sir.

03:38.510 --> 03:41.138
- Come on up. Up. Okay, that's it.
- One, two.

03:41.221 --> 03:42.222
Stop.

03:45.851 --> 03:47.394
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun!

03:48.019 --> 03:49.271
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun...

03:50.689 --> 03:52.065
Time's up, sir.

03:52.232 --> 03:53.233
Really?

03:53.316 --> 03:54.526
So I can get out now?

03:55.861 --> 03:57.070
No, that's not it.

03:57.154 --> 03:58.196
Stop messing around

03:58.280 --> 04:01.450
and let me out too!

04:24.306 --> 04:26.558
Frying proficiency has increased.

04:26.641 --> 04:27.851
Level up.

04:29.436 --> 04:30.437
Yes!

04:34.858 --> 04:37.235
Look at you, it's a party over here,
Kang Seong-jae.

04:37.319 --> 04:38.528
Private Kang Seong-jae!

04:38.612 --> 04:40.530
The fried food turned out well, sir.

04:40.614 --> 04:41.865
Oh, is that so?

04:41.948 --> 04:42.949
I see.

04:43.742 --> 04:45.076
Well then

04:45.160 --> 04:46.787
keep frying delicious food from now on

04:46.870 --> 04:48.997
stir-frying, boiling, do it all.

04:49.247 --> 04:51.666
Yes, sir. I'll really do my best.

04:52.751 --> 04:54.669
What am I going to do with you?

04:56.004 --> 04:57.464
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun, thank you.

04:57.839 --> 04:59.758
When I was on leave helping my mom

04:59.841 --> 05:01.927
I came like I had a lot to learn.

05:03.512 --> 05:06.765
Army food and civilian food
are worlds apart.

05:07.015 --> 05:09.267
It doesn't matter
if it's tasty for army grunts.

05:09.351 --> 05:10.644
As long as it's fried

05:10.727 --> 05:11.770
they just go crazy and...

05:12.729 --> 05:15.106
They just stuff their faces, you know?

05:15.440 --> 05:17.567
Do you think this would taste good

05:17.651 --> 05:19.444
if you had it outside?

05:24.825 --> 05:25.826
What's this?

05:27.077 --> 05:29.746
It's crispier than before his leave.

05:32.499 --> 05:33.500
Lanterns.

05:34.417 --> 05:35.919
- Lanterns, check.
- Lanterns, check.

05:37.587 --> 05:39.047
Every one of these checks

05:39.130 --> 05:41.383
can mean life and death

05:41.466 --> 05:43.802
so let's prepare thoroughly. Understood?

05:43.969 --> 05:45.554
- Yes, ma'am!
- Yes, ma'am!

05:46.555 --> 05:49.558
- Shovels.
- They didn't seem like just friends.

05:51.017 --> 05:52.477
I'm not sure what you mean, sir.

05:53.895 --> 05:55.021
I'm talking about Major Im
and Outpost Commander Cho.

05:56.690 --> 05:58.066
From what I hear

05:58.149 --> 06:00.569
since they were at the outpost

06:01.403 --> 06:03.363
there's been something
going on between them.

06:06.241 --> 06:07.784
Oh, is that so?

06:08.618 --> 06:10.579
You work with them
and you didn't know that?

06:11.746 --> 06:12.998
I'm sorry, sir.

06:14.374 --> 06:15.876
I just, well...

06:16.543 --> 06:18.712
I just thought they were close.

06:23.466 --> 06:24.467
Seok-ho.

06:24.968 --> 06:25.969
Yes, Battalion Commander.

06:27.470 --> 06:28.471
Look.

06:29.472 --> 06:31.600
I'm telling you this for your own good.

06:31.892 --> 06:34.352
if you get involved
with deadweights like her out of pity

06:34.769 --> 06:36.146
you'll just get dragged into their mess.

06:37.439 --> 06:40.191
The ones getting discharged
will be gone soon on their own.

06:40.859 --> 06:42.694
So don't worry about her too much.

06:43.153 --> 06:44.446
Just...

06:44.779 --> 06:46.323
make sure you don't cross any lines.

06:49.534 --> 06:51.202
I'm worried about you.

06:51.286 --> 06:52.287
You.

07:01.755 --> 07:02.839
Okay, okay.

07:04.799 --> 07:05.967
I mean...

07:06.051 --> 07:07.469
can we really cook with this?

07:08.011 --> 07:09.512
Of course, huh?

07:09.596 --> 07:11.056
We use this to cook rice

07:11.139 --> 07:12.140
make side dishes

07:12.307 --> 07:14.142
basically anything that needs a fire.

07:14.225 --> 07:15.393
What century are we in?

07:15.477 --> 07:17.354
You can just microwave rice.

07:17.437 --> 07:19.522
Hey, I can hear you!

07:19.606 --> 07:20.941
You think KCTC is a joke?

07:21.274 --> 07:24.486
This training is set up to be exactly
like a real wartime situation.

07:24.861 --> 07:26.029
Last training

07:26.112 --> 07:27.697
the cooks abandoned the kitchen trailer

07:27.781 --> 07:30.492
and we ate nothing but hardtack
until the training was over. Jeez.

07:30.575 --> 07:32.410
The moment that happens

07:32.494 --> 07:33.995
you'll be up for disciplinary action.

07:34.079 --> 07:35.163
Even if...

07:35.705 --> 07:37.749
the moment comes for you
to die a glorious death

07:37.832 --> 07:39.292
you must sacrifice yourselves

07:39.376 --> 07:41.544
and protect this truck. You hear me?

07:42.045 --> 07:44.381
What... what do you mean by that?

07:44.714 --> 07:46.383
Are you saying we could actually die?

07:47.634 --> 07:48.927
Did you think KCTC

07:49.094 --> 07:50.887
was make-believe like other drills?

07:51.137 --> 07:53.056
This is on a whole other level.

07:53.723 --> 07:54.975
A different level.

08:06.236 --> 08:07.779
From this moment on

08:07.862 --> 08:09.739
you're in a training state.

08:09.990 --> 08:13.159
When a signal is sent to the sensor
attached to a firearm

08:13.451 --> 08:15.203
an alert will appear on MILES gear

08:15.286 --> 08:16.871
that you are wearing.

08:16.955 --> 08:19.624
It will report where, by whom

08:19.708 --> 08:20.959
and how many shots you took

08:21.084 --> 08:23.336
leading to serious injury or death.

08:23.670 --> 08:25.463
Just like in actual combat

08:25.547 --> 08:26.881
you'll be carried off by medics

08:26.965 --> 08:28.675
and removed from the exercise.

08:29.134 --> 08:30.218
Make sure that doesn't happen.

08:30.301 --> 08:32.303
A cook has to fire a gun?

08:32.762 --> 08:34.472
That means things have gone
as bad as they can get

08:34.931 --> 08:37.809
so we should surrender peacefully. Got it?

08:38.101 --> 08:40.145
Have you forgotten
what the Master Sergeant said?

08:40.562 --> 08:42.939
He told us to protect the kitchen trailer

08:43.023 --> 08:44.566
even if it means dying.

08:44.774 --> 08:46.276
Why are you so dramatic?

08:46.359 --> 08:47.402
Just take it easy, man.

08:50.488 --> 08:51.531
Yes, sir.

08:51.614 --> 08:53.283
Dig along here. Here, like this.

08:53.408 --> 08:54.784
Like this.

08:59.039 --> 09:00.040
Goodness.

09:00.498 --> 09:03.418
I don't know if I'm making a meal
or becoming one.

09:04.085 --> 09:06.546
How long does it take
to get a fire started?

09:06.629 --> 09:07.630
Hey.

09:07.922 --> 09:09.257
Look at those kitchen slackers.

09:09.924 --> 09:12.427
They're used to having it easy,
but now that they have to cook outside

09:12.510 --> 09:13.928
they're completely lost.

09:14.137 --> 09:16.389
- But can you cook with that junk?
- What do you think?

09:18.767 --> 09:19.809
Come on, light.

09:41.081 --> 09:42.082
Salute!

09:42.165 --> 09:43.166
Salute!

09:44.250 --> 09:45.251
Are the preparations going well?

09:45.335 --> 09:46.836
No problems so far, sir.

09:46.920 --> 09:49.714
The Commander saw your evaluation
and has high expectations.

09:53.468 --> 09:56.346
Seok-ho, you have to deliver
this time to score big.

09:57.305 --> 09:58.890
- You're confident, aren't you?
- Absolutely, sir.

09:59.349 --> 10:00.350
I am Hwang Seok-ho.

10:00.683 --> 10:02.268
- You can count on me.
- Excellent.

10:11.694 --> 10:14.906
Warning. Maintain a high flame.

10:16.699 --> 10:18.368
I'm trying to.

10:19.410 --> 10:20.495
This is the best I can do.

10:20.578 --> 10:21.871
Man, I'm starving.

10:22.080 --> 10:23.206
Hey, look at this!

10:23.289 --> 10:24.999
Goodness, these guys...

10:25.375 --> 10:28.419
Are they gonna wait
until we starve to feed us? Huh?

10:28.503 --> 10:30.505
Can't you see everyone's waiting on you?

10:30.588 --> 10:32.757
Master Sergeant, we've been trying

10:32.841 --> 10:34.467
just to light this cauldron.

10:34.551 --> 10:36.094
What's with the excuses?

10:36.177 --> 10:38.096
Guys before you managed to light it.

10:38.346 --> 10:40.223
Due to the old kitchen trailer...

10:40.306 --> 10:42.308
SPICY BRAISED CHICKEN MADE
IN OLD KITCHEN TRAILER, REEKS OF GREASE

10:42.392 --> 10:45.812
The star rating
for spicy braised chicken has dropped.

11:00.285 --> 11:01.911
Gosh, that greasy smell.

11:02.245 --> 11:04.414
This smells so much like motor oil,
it could probably start an engine.

11:04.706 --> 11:07.375
On top of that, the rice is
undercooked and hard, sir.

11:07.959 --> 11:09.085
We're sorry.

11:11.421 --> 11:12.422
Cooks!

11:13.631 --> 11:15.175
- Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.
- Cooks, freeze!

11:17.510 --> 11:19.095
You call this food?

11:19.262 --> 11:21.181
Sir, we tried

11:21.264 --> 11:22.682
but the exhaust fan is just so old.

11:22.765 --> 11:24.767
It was difficult to stop
the grease from leaking, sir.

11:24.851 --> 11:27.145
A true soldier doesn't blame his gear.

11:27.729 --> 11:30.523
Do you have any idea how important
provisions are in combat?

11:30.940 --> 11:33.693
With morale this low,
how can we expect to be winners!

11:34.944 --> 11:35.945
We're sorry, sir.

11:36.529 --> 11:38.114
I, Hwang Seok-ho

11:38.198 --> 11:40.158
will not let this slide.

11:40.241 --> 11:41.242
I'll make sure

11:41.326 --> 11:43.161
you're accountable after this drill.

11:43.661 --> 11:44.954
- Yoon Dong-hyun.
- Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

11:45.038 --> 11:46.414
- Kang Seong-jae.
- Private Kang Seong-jae.

11:50.919 --> 11:52.253
Oh, man...

11:56.716 --> 11:57.967
My apologies, Battalion Commander.

11:58.051 --> 11:59.469
The food is awful.

11:59.761 --> 12:00.803
Look.

12:00.887 --> 12:02.555
Is this a time to be picky
about food? This is war.

12:02.764 --> 12:03.765
The rice may be a little off

12:03.848 --> 12:05.225
but the meat makes it a solid meal.

12:06.017 --> 12:07.018
But strangely

12:07.560 --> 12:09.270
my stomach is starting
to hurt a little, sir.

12:10.855 --> 12:12.732
If it's good, just say so.

12:12.815 --> 12:14.317
Stop messing around.

12:19.530 --> 12:20.698
I don't think he's messing around.

12:30.416 --> 12:31.793
Battalion... Battalion Commander...

12:35.171 --> 12:36.214
Private First Class Tak Mun-ik!

12:38.132 --> 12:39.133
Battalion Commander!

12:41.302 --> 12:42.387
Hey, stop fooling around.

12:42.470 --> 12:43.554
I'm not fooling around!

12:46.266 --> 12:47.475
Please help me.

12:47.558 --> 12:48.768
Help me.

12:49.769 --> 12:53.356
I think I'm really gonna crap my pants!

12:54.399 --> 12:55.483
What is happening?

12:55.566 --> 12:56.567
Hey.

12:56.651 --> 12:58.569
This isn't part of the drill, is it?

13:05.451 --> 13:07.161
- Salute!
- Salute!

13:07.245 --> 13:08.454
Salute!

13:11.374 --> 13:13.376
Damn it, seriously!

13:14.294 --> 13:16.879
I think this has gotten
pretty serious, sir.

13:19.841 --> 13:21.467
I don't care if it's a drill or not.

13:21.551 --> 13:23.428
How did you cook so poorly
that everyone got food poisoning!

13:23.553 --> 13:24.595
I'm sorry?

13:25.054 --> 13:26.180
Food Poisoning?

13:26.556 --> 13:27.557
That can't be.

13:27.640 --> 13:29.559
How can you say that
after looking at them?

13:35.690 --> 13:37.025
In my division...

13:37.692 --> 13:39.360
something like this should never happen.

13:40.528 --> 13:41.529
I'm sorry, sir.

13:43.990 --> 13:46.659
All that praise must have gone
to your head.

13:51.581 --> 13:52.582
Get up. Both of you.

13:53.041 --> 13:54.083
- Getting up!
- Getting up!

13:54.292 --> 13:55.460
- Hey.
- Getting up!

13:56.336 --> 13:59.213
To be safe, we're throwing out
all the remaining food supplies.

13:59.297 --> 14:02.050
Until the next supplies arrive,
we'll survive on combat rations.

14:02.133 --> 14:03.384
Master Sergeant.

14:03.676 --> 14:05.011
This is really unfair to us.

14:05.094 --> 14:06.387
Unfair? Don't be ridiculous.

14:06.471 --> 14:08.681
Everyone's got a stomachache.

14:08.765 --> 14:10.350
The only thing they ate was the chicken.

14:10.433 --> 14:12.477
We boiled the chicken for a long time.

14:12.560 --> 14:14.270
We washed the pot two or three times.

14:15.146 --> 14:17.482
If it's Food Poisoning, Sergeant
Yoon Dong-hyun and Kang Seong-jae

14:17.565 --> 14:20.234
will be hauled off for training
after this exercise, won't they?

14:20.318 --> 14:22.278
Yep. You know

14:22.820 --> 14:24.238
I can't stand people who mess around

14:24.322 --> 14:25.323
when it comes to food.

14:25.656 --> 14:27.075
Guys like that need to be taught a lesson.

14:28.368 --> 14:29.619
I hope they get their leave canceled.

14:29.744 --> 14:31.204
Isn't that a little harsh?

14:31.454 --> 14:32.705
We had our food taken away too...

14:33.706 --> 14:34.707
by them.

14:52.183 --> 14:53.559
Enemy position acquired.

14:54.018 --> 14:55.645
Requesting fire support
on these coordinates.

15:10.076 --> 15:12.286
Activating the Chef's Eye.

15:23.840 --> 15:26.092
Hey, hey, hey!

15:26.175 --> 15:27.176
Are you crazy?

15:27.260 --> 15:30.012
Are you trying to get food poisoning
so you can drop out?

15:30.346 --> 15:33.307
I don't think
there's anything wrong with the food.

15:33.516 --> 15:36.352
What, so you're going to be
the official food taster now?

15:37.061 --> 15:38.729
I mean, even for you,
in a situation like this

15:38.813 --> 15:40.606
wouldn't it be weirder
if you didn't get sick?

15:40.815 --> 15:43.651
For all we know, it could be
from that rice that reeks of oil.

15:44.402 --> 15:46.654
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun,
don't you think this is unfair?

15:46.863 --> 15:48.281
This isn't even our fault.

15:49.824 --> 15:52.410
You know what the most useless
feeling in the army is?

15:52.743 --> 15:53.828
Feeling wronged.

15:54.036 --> 15:55.621
So what if I feel wronged? Who cares?

15:56.330 --> 15:57.665
This is so frustrating.

15:57.748 --> 15:59.208
- What is that?
- Killed.

15:59.417 --> 16:00.793
What? What was that?

16:00.877 --> 16:02.044
- Killed.
- What is that?

16:02.128 --> 16:03.337
Killed.

16:03.421 --> 16:04.922
Enemy shell incoming!

16:05.006 --> 16:06.716
Enemy shell incoming!

16:06.799 --> 16:08.426
It's an attack from the opposing force.

16:08.509 --> 16:09.844
- Yeah, get down!
- Get down.

16:11.053 --> 16:12.513
Hey, take cover!

16:12.597 --> 16:14.557
What? What happened? Why?

16:14.640 --> 16:15.808
How did he die? How?

16:16.684 --> 16:18.769
We received the signal
for an artillery strike, now.

16:19.103 --> 16:20.646
If we don't move to a base camp

16:20.730 --> 16:22.106
the remaining soldiers are at risk.

16:22.899 --> 16:24.817
Oh, just look at this mess.

16:25.443 --> 16:27.612
This way. Form up over here.

16:29.238 --> 16:30.239
This way.

16:31.991 --> 16:33.242
- Thank you.
- Form two lines.

16:33.951 --> 16:35.036
What should we do?

16:35.620 --> 16:37.538
What do you mean? We have to move.

16:39.749 --> 16:42.418
Move out! Leave the tents.

16:42.502 --> 16:44.212
- Move out!
- Move!

16:44.295 --> 16:45.546
Move!

16:45.630 --> 16:47.715
And he's supposed to be our commander.

16:48.257 --> 16:50.343
Survivors, hurry, hurry!

16:50.676 --> 16:51.761
This is for real!

16:53.346 --> 16:54.722
Count off!

16:54.805 --> 16:56.891
- One, two, three, four...
- One, two, three, four...

16:56.974 --> 16:58.059
Five. All clear.

16:58.518 --> 16:59.519
At this rate...

16:59.602 --> 17:02.021
are we all going to die?

17:02.813 --> 17:03.814
Don't chicken out!

17:04.065 --> 17:05.358
It's not like we're actually going to die.

17:06.651 --> 17:07.902
Move the trailer!

17:08.069 --> 17:09.070
Yes, sir!

17:11.197 --> 17:12.240
Give it here, quick!

17:12.907 --> 17:13.908
Faster!

17:38.766 --> 17:39.767
Halt.

17:43.646 --> 17:45.856
We'll set up the base camp here.

17:46.524 --> 17:47.775
Everyone, spread out

17:47.858 --> 17:49.193
and secure the perimeter. Stay sharp.

17:49.360 --> 17:50.736
Keep your voices down.

17:50.820 --> 17:51.821
Understand?

17:51.904 --> 17:53.239
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

17:53.656 --> 17:55.658
All right. Outpost Commander,
Deputy Outpost Commander. Step forward.

18:05.960 --> 18:06.961
Warning.

18:07.044 --> 18:08.713
Morale is falling.

18:10.047 --> 18:12.633
Current survivor count is at 47%.

18:13.384 --> 18:15.344
Morale is at 29%.

18:18.431 --> 18:19.849
To boost morale

18:20.099 --> 18:22.602
you must satisfy the soldiers' hunger.

18:51.839 --> 18:52.840
Corporal Joo Sang-uk!

18:54.550 --> 18:55.551
Corporal Joo Sang-uk!

18:56.802 --> 18:58.512
- What?
- There's something over there.

19:01.724 --> 19:02.725
Jeez.

19:02.808 --> 19:04.727
It's so dark I can't see a thing.

19:06.228 --> 19:07.980
Can't you see that silhouette over there?

19:13.194 --> 19:14.445
I see it.

19:14.528 --> 19:16.155
I think it's getting closer.

19:16.447 --> 19:17.448
Stop!

19:17.531 --> 19:18.532
Move and I'll shoot.

19:19.033 --> 19:20.242
Are you a civilian?

19:24.747 --> 19:27.124
I'm here for the food waste bin.

19:33.964 --> 19:35.633
It's the food waste bin man. Hey.

19:36.676 --> 19:39.261
Still, we shouldn't let him in.

19:39.345 --> 19:40.554
- We should at least report this...
- Hey.

19:40.971 --> 19:43.015
We ask for the password,
and if he doesn't know, we send him away?

19:43.099 --> 19:44.266
Then who's going to empty the scraps?

19:46.852 --> 19:47.978
Open the gate. Hurry.

19:51.023 --> 19:52.108
- Come on in.
- Oh, thanks.

19:58.364 --> 19:59.782
- Thank you.
- Sure.

20:05.621 --> 20:07.873
Hey. Cover me for a bit.

20:23.347 --> 20:24.473
I'm here for the food waste bin.

20:31.772 --> 20:33.149
Did you light the fire?

20:33.566 --> 20:34.567
Not yet.

20:34.650 --> 20:37.653
You can't even get a fire started?
What are you looking at?

20:37.737 --> 20:39.780
Being out in the field
has you all messed up, huh?

20:39.864 --> 20:41.157
- Move!
- Yes, sir.

20:44.243 --> 20:45.786
But, Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun...

20:46.579 --> 20:47.788
Doesn't this seem a little strange?

20:48.080 --> 20:49.498
Everything's strange.

20:49.874 --> 20:51.751
Is there anything that isn't strange?

20:52.084 --> 20:54.211
We haven't slept.
What the hell are we even doing?

20:54.295 --> 20:57.840
Are civilians allowed to enter
during a training exercise?

20:58.048 --> 20:59.717
Scraps are about to overflow.

20:59.800 --> 21:01.427
Are we supposed to leave it like that?

21:01.510 --> 21:02.511
MORALE IS RISING

21:02.595 --> 21:04.263
But he looks too suspicious

21:04.346 --> 21:05.765
to be just a civilian.

21:05.848 --> 21:07.391
Just drop it.

21:11.020 --> 21:12.021
Wait.

21:13.606 --> 21:14.607
Hands up!

21:14.690 --> 21:15.691
Move and I'll shoot.

21:16.317 --> 21:17.610
Hey, Mr. Soldiers.

21:17.693 --> 21:19.945
The guys at the front let me in.

21:20.029 --> 21:21.363
Cactus.

21:21.447 --> 21:23.491
Cactus... Why a cactus?

21:24.492 --> 21:25.826
Are you really a civilian?

21:30.247 --> 21:31.832
- Hey, hey.
- Kang Seong-jae.

21:32.333 --> 21:33.334
He's...

21:34.919 --> 21:35.920
What's going on?

21:36.128 --> 21:37.838
He seems suspicious.

21:38.088 --> 21:39.799
What is your problem?

21:40.549 --> 21:44.303
You talked to the guards at the gate
before coming in, right?

21:44.553 --> 21:45.805
- See?
- Then...

21:46.055 --> 21:48.974
show me what you were just about to
take out of your pocket.

21:51.519 --> 21:52.895
-What?
-What are you doing?

21:52.978 --> 21:54.188
You're scaring him.

21:54.271 --> 21:57.983
We are conducting this training
as if it were a real situation.

21:58.692 --> 21:59.902
If you don't mind...

22:00.277 --> 22:03.197
could we see what's in your pocket?

22:09.870 --> 22:10.871
Yoon Dong-hyun.

22:11.705 --> 22:13.249
Jeez, what could the food waste bin man

22:13.332 --> 22:14.542
possibly have in his pocket?

22:20.464 --> 22:21.590
What? Is this...

22:21.674 --> 22:22.716
a detonator?

22:25.177 --> 22:27.221
Damn it, I was so close.

22:30.099 --> 22:31.767
Infiltrator detected.

22:32.768 --> 22:34.979
Since you've been discovered,
we're going to search you.

22:38.899 --> 22:39.984
Hands up.

22:41.819 --> 22:44.780
A hidden opposing force officer
has been discovered.

22:45.155 --> 22:47.867
Morale increased by 5%.

22:59.336 --> 23:01.005
Even if this is just a drill

23:01.088 --> 23:02.172
how could you...

23:02.381 --> 23:04.049
let a spy disguised as a civilian

23:04.133 --> 23:05.509
just walk right in?

23:06.886 --> 23:10.306
The enemy is looking for
any way to neutralize us

23:10.472 --> 23:13.267
and you think you can get away
with being this careless?

23:25.487 --> 23:27.573
- Battalion Commander.
- Damn it.

23:34.330 --> 23:35.789
You guys should be ashamed of yourselves.

23:36.332 --> 23:37.833
Because you were negligent on watch

23:38.083 --> 23:39.752
The Regimental Commander is furious.

23:39.835 --> 23:40.961
Especially you two. Damn it.

23:41.295 --> 23:43.380
Are you trying to bring down
the whole unit?

23:44.048 --> 23:45.090
- I'm sorry.
- I'm sorry.

23:45.299 --> 23:47.051
Corporal Joo Sang-uk
said it was okay, so I...

23:47.134 --> 23:48.177
When did I say that?

23:48.260 --> 23:49.261
Watch your mouth.

23:49.428 --> 23:51.931
Regardless, you're his senior.
Shouldn't you take responsibility?

23:52.640 --> 23:54.892
Forget it. Your disciplinary
action is confirmed

23:55.267 --> 23:58.479
so write up a written statement
and bring it to me. Got it?

23:58.562 --> 23:59.563
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

23:59.647 --> 24:01.607
I can't hear you. I said, got it?

24:01.690 --> 24:02.691
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

24:06.278 --> 24:08.405
This is a map we obtained
from a captured enemy.

24:08.697 --> 24:10.157
It seems they're trying to infiltrate

24:10.240 --> 24:12.034
from the nearest location.

24:12.534 --> 24:13.535
Good job.

24:14.495 --> 24:16.080
If it weren't for you,
we would've been finished.

24:16.330 --> 24:17.331
Thank you.

24:17.581 --> 24:18.749
The company worked day and night

24:18.832 --> 24:21.085
giving their all to this drill.

24:21.168 --> 24:22.211
That's how we achieved...

24:22.294 --> 24:23.963
For now, let's focus on guarding
against the opposing force.

24:24.171 --> 24:26.924
Those punks will do anything
to rush our main base.

24:27.549 --> 24:29.468
We don't have many soldiers left

24:29.551 --> 24:30.552
so do not die.

24:30.636 --> 24:32.513
If any of you die before I do

24:33.389 --> 24:35.182
you'll have me to answer to.

24:36.100 --> 24:37.101
Got it?

24:37.184 --> 24:38.268
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

24:38.602 --> 24:39.687
These punks...

24:42.606 --> 24:44.108
Don't die before me...

24:45.359 --> 24:46.360
Not again.

24:53.909 --> 24:56.412
At this rate, I'm really gonna die
before this drill is over.

25:07.631 --> 25:08.632
Killed.

25:08.716 --> 25:09.717
Killed.

25:09.800 --> 25:10.801
Killed.

25:17.725 --> 25:20.561
With over 70% of our troops
counted as dead

25:20.644 --> 25:22.438
the outcome is looking grim.

25:27.985 --> 25:30.279
It's only been two days,
and it's already a disaster.

25:30.571 --> 25:32.364
What in the world have you been doing?

25:33.323 --> 25:35.617
Keep the remaining men alive
and hold out, no matter what.

25:35.826 --> 25:37.119
No matter what!

25:37.202 --> 25:38.203
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

25:40.247 --> 25:41.248
By the way...

25:41.582 --> 25:43.542
Where is the Battalion Commander
and what is he doing?

26:11.820 --> 26:13.781
The Battalion Commander was killed

26:13.864 --> 26:15.532
so I'm in charge of the battalion.

26:15.866 --> 26:17.868
In a situation like this, do not panic.

26:18.160 --> 26:20.287
I expect each of you to do your best
in your assigned positions.

26:20.370 --> 26:21.872
He told us to be careful

26:21.955 --> 26:23.916
and then he goes and dies first.

26:24.541 --> 26:26.293
Cold-blooded bastards.

26:26.627 --> 26:28.462
- No one's tough taking a dump.
- Salute.

26:30.506 --> 26:32.883
The supply vehicle was attacked
making it difficult to distribute rations.

26:33.050 --> 26:34.718
We are to switch to combat rations,
effective immediately.

26:36.720 --> 26:38.013
Seriously, in this situation...

26:38.305 --> 26:39.890
What are we supposed to do
if our supplies are cut off?

26:47.481 --> 26:49.441
Looks like we'll get to go home
early today.

26:49.525 --> 26:51.735
It makes it easy for us
when they just die on their own.

26:51.819 --> 26:52.945
We've cut off their supply line

26:53.028 --> 26:54.363
so they're probably having a meltdown.

26:54.446 --> 26:55.531
They need to be taught a lesson.

26:55.614 --> 26:57.282
They have no military discipline.

26:57.366 --> 26:58.826
They're a complete circus.

26:59.243 --> 27:00.244
All right, listen up!

27:01.286 --> 27:02.996
We're now advancing into Sector B.

27:03.997 --> 27:06.333
If that plainclothes op had worked,
we wouldn't be here.

27:06.416 --> 27:07.709
If we head to their location

27:07.793 --> 27:09.586
we can wipe out their forces.

27:09.670 --> 27:11.213
Let's hang in there a little longer.
All right?

27:11.380 --> 27:12.589
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

27:16.552 --> 27:17.845
Oh, damn it.

27:19.012 --> 27:20.013
Jeez.

27:23.892 --> 27:24.893
Oh, man.

27:26.645 --> 27:29.481
Use of the kitchen trailer
has been suspended.

27:31.024 --> 27:32.776
Hey, you punk!
I told you to tow it carefully

27:32.860 --> 27:34.278
not wreck it!

27:34.778 --> 27:36.530
To be honest, Master Sergeant

27:36.613 --> 27:38.782
would it have been that surprising
if this thing broke down?

27:38.866 --> 27:39.867
For crying out loud...

27:40.909 --> 27:42.327
Oh, goodness.

27:43.162 --> 27:44.621
I don't know what to do anymore.

27:45.455 --> 27:47.499
From now on keep fire to a minimum.

27:47.666 --> 27:48.667
Yes, sir.

27:49.001 --> 27:52.129
Why is this pound cake always so dry?

27:52.588 --> 27:54.965
Man, an iced Americano
would really hit the spot right now.

27:56.258 --> 27:57.259
Cook.

27:57.718 --> 27:59.094
Think I can get a cup of coffee?

28:15.569 --> 28:17.487
They look like a defeated army.

28:17.988 --> 28:18.989
Tell me about it.

28:19.323 --> 28:21.450
Everyone eat up and don't leave
any leftovers. Got it?

28:21.617 --> 28:23.243
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

28:27.247 --> 28:28.248
Guys.

28:29.666 --> 28:31.001
How much food do we have left?

28:31.084 --> 28:32.711
Our supply route has been cut off...

28:33.587 --> 28:36.131
and I'm not sure what we have
is enough to last.

28:36.298 --> 28:38.050
All food supplies were disposed of

28:38.133 --> 28:39.551
so we have no replacements.

28:40.469 --> 28:41.845
We have orders from high command

28:41.929 --> 28:43.889
to substitute with combat rations

28:44.389 --> 28:45.515
If this keeps up

28:45.599 --> 28:47.392
it's going to take
a physical toll on everyone.

28:50.145 --> 28:52.105
Use the ingredients in the supply vehicle

28:52.189 --> 28:53.815
to create a meal.

28:56.902 --> 28:57.903
Outpost Commander.

28:58.487 --> 28:59.488
By any chance...

28:59.863 --> 29:02.324
do you know the last known location
of the supply vehicle?

29:03.700 --> 29:05.577
It's not far from here.

29:05.994 --> 29:06.995
Why?

29:07.079 --> 29:08.497
If it's not far

29:08.580 --> 29:10.415
wouldn't it be better
to go there ourselves?

29:10.540 --> 29:12.376
The sun's about to set.

29:12.459 --> 29:14.211
You want to move out and get killed?

29:15.504 --> 29:16.505
That's a good point.

29:16.588 --> 29:19.466
The opposing force didn't have
the resources to move the supplies.

29:20.133 --> 29:23.136
If we go and retrieve
the leftover supplies...

29:23.845 --> 29:25.430
Not you too, Outpost Commander?

29:25.514 --> 29:27.224
Do you think this makes any sense?

29:27.391 --> 29:28.809
If we leave our posts

29:28.892 --> 29:30.477
who's going to take responsibility?

29:30.644 --> 29:33.272
- We have to do everything we can.
- What?

29:33.355 --> 29:35.482
I don't want to die. Damn it!

29:37.526 --> 29:39.319
We need your help, Master Sergeant.

29:39.987 --> 29:41.238
You will help us, won't you?

30:09.433 --> 30:11.643
I can't see a thing.
I have no idea where we are.

30:11.977 --> 30:13.812
I think it was somewhere around here.

30:24.906 --> 30:25.949
This way.

30:27.034 --> 30:28.618
Can we trust you on that?

30:30.537 --> 30:32.289
All my years of service
weren't for nothing.

30:33.999 --> 30:35.167
Just trust me and follow my lead.

31:01.860 --> 31:02.986
See? Told you I was right.

31:03.070 --> 31:04.279
This is the way.

31:07.324 --> 31:08.408
Master Sergeant.

31:08.742 --> 31:10.744
I don't think they've seen us yet.

31:11.078 --> 31:12.913
Shouldn't we just turn back now?

31:14.039 --> 31:15.332
But we've come this far.

31:15.415 --> 31:17.459
It'd be a waste to just turn back.

31:18.293 --> 31:20.295
It's not going to be easy
for the four of us.

31:21.880 --> 31:23.715
Once a soldier draws his weapon

31:24.257 --> 31:25.926
he has to see it through
to the end, right?

31:27.260 --> 31:28.261
Dong-hyun.

31:28.887 --> 31:30.555
Why... why are you calling me, sir?

31:31.473 --> 31:32.766
Ah, hell...

31:33.642 --> 31:35.560
Master Sergeant...

31:52.786 --> 31:54.704
Eat lead, Vipers!

31:57.833 --> 31:59.876
Judging by how they flinch

31:59.960 --> 32:02.003
they're not the Vipers, but Earthworms!

32:02.087 --> 32:03.422
Stop trying to steal our dinner!

32:03.505 --> 32:04.506
Come and get it!

32:04.589 --> 32:06.758
Yeah, bring it on, Earthworms.

32:07.968 --> 32:09.177
Who the hell are those guys?

32:09.261 --> 32:10.637
All right, now run!

32:10.887 --> 32:11.930
I'll go first, sir!

32:12.013 --> 32:13.265
Run like hell!

32:14.141 --> 32:15.809
Run faster than you thought possible!

32:16.143 --> 32:17.185
Faster!

32:17.811 --> 32:19.104
I can still see your feet!

32:19.187 --> 32:20.856
- They're crazy, sir.
- Faster than anyone!

32:21.106 --> 32:22.816
I said run like this!

32:22.899 --> 32:24.192
Bring it on!

32:24.276 --> 32:25.277
Faster than anyone.

32:27.320 --> 32:28.780
You can't see my feet, can you?

32:28.864 --> 32:29.865
Yeah!

32:31.241 --> 32:32.617
Faster than anyone.

32:32.701 --> 32:33.952
You Earthworms.

32:38.081 --> 32:39.499
Outpost Commander, now!

32:41.042 --> 32:42.210
Hey, let's move.

32:42.711 --> 32:43.712
Yes, sir.

32:53.346 --> 32:55.474
Killed.

32:55.557 --> 32:56.850
- Killed.
- What?

32:57.601 --> 32:59.895
Killed.

33:34.846 --> 33:35.847
Killed.

33:36.223 --> 33:37.224
Killed.

33:44.689 --> 33:45.941
I told you.

33:46.525 --> 33:48.318
All my years of service
weren't for nothing.

33:48.652 --> 33:49.861
Master Sergeant!

33:55.992 --> 33:57.035
Three, four...

33:57.786 --> 33:58.787
Still...

33:58.870 --> 34:00.789
I think this should be
more than enough for us.

34:00.872 --> 34:03.708
A little underwhelming
for something we risked lives for.

34:04.084 --> 34:06.753
Master Sergeant,
you're faster than I thought.

34:07.254 --> 34:09.881
Hey, kid. It's only 'cause
I'm getting old and stiff.

34:09.965 --> 34:12.008
In my day, I'd be doing somersaults

34:12.092 --> 34:14.553
all over the place!

34:14.928 --> 34:17.305
I'm glad everyone made it back unhurt.

34:19.432 --> 34:20.684
I'm very proud.

34:21.476 --> 34:22.477
Hey, Cho Ye-rin!

34:27.732 --> 34:29.442
Who gave you permission
to take the men and move out?

34:29.776 --> 34:31.611
We don't know when supplies come.

34:31.695 --> 34:32.904
Are we supposed to sit here and wait?

34:32.988 --> 34:36.157
Any follow-up action still needs
a commander's approval.

34:36.866 --> 34:38.743
The soldiers are starving.

34:38.827 --> 34:40.912
- I couldn't just stand by and wait.
- Hey.

34:41.997 --> 34:43.415
You've got an answer
for everything, don't you?

34:44.207 --> 34:45.834
Our temporary Battalion Commander.

34:46.334 --> 34:48.378
You're really getting into this
"playing Battalion Commander," huh?

34:49.045 --> 34:50.046
Hey, Company Commander.

34:50.922 --> 34:52.215
How can you say that
in a wartime situation?

34:52.424 --> 34:53.842
"Hey, Company Commander"? "Hey"?

34:54.342 --> 34:55.343
This is ridiculous.

34:55.677 --> 34:56.803
Hey, Battalion Commander.

34:56.886 --> 34:58.346
So what's your plan now?

34:58.805 --> 35:01.349
We can't make a move
until you give us a plan.

35:01.433 --> 35:02.976
And after everyone went through hell
to get those supplies.

35:03.059 --> 35:04.102
What is all this?

35:04.811 --> 35:05.812
- Salute.
- Salute.

35:05.979 --> 35:07.188
- At ease.
- Salute!

35:08.732 --> 35:09.733
Battalion Commander.

35:10.150 --> 35:11.484
How did you make it back, sir?

35:11.651 --> 35:12.902
What do you mean, "how"?

35:12.986 --> 35:14.654
You'd think I actually died.

35:15.488 --> 35:17.616
Sides have switched, and as of now

35:17.699 --> 35:19.034
the death count is reset.

35:19.743 --> 35:20.910
That's a huge relief, sir.

35:21.494 --> 35:22.871
Is your stomach better, sir?

35:22.954 --> 35:24.122
Don't worry about me.

35:24.205 --> 35:25.206
So what happened?

35:25.540 --> 35:27.626
While I was filling in for you,
Battalion Commander

35:27.959 --> 35:30.003
The Outpost Commander
moved troops without reporting.

35:33.131 --> 35:34.674
I judged it'd take a toll on soldiers

35:34.758 --> 35:36.301
if we stayed put.

35:36.384 --> 35:37.886
Even so.

35:38.386 --> 35:39.804
Without reporting
during a wartime situation?

35:40.096 --> 35:41.514
Is that acceptable?

35:43.808 --> 35:44.809
Regarding this...

35:45.352 --> 35:46.603
as soon as this training is over

35:47.228 --> 35:48.480
submit a written statement.

35:49.939 --> 35:50.982
Understand?

35:51.650 --> 35:53.443
Yes, sir.

35:59.866 --> 36:00.867
Seriously?

36:01.868 --> 36:04.704
So we're just supposed to
wait here and starve?

36:05.205 --> 36:07.749
If this was a real wartime situation,
none of this would fly.

36:07.832 --> 36:11.378
The Battalion Commander from the dead
wouldn't fly either, sir.

36:12.253 --> 36:14.673
We ran our butts off to get here,
and instead of a "good job"

36:14.756 --> 36:16.299
we get a written statement? Seriously?

36:18.760 --> 36:20.136
Is everyone okay? Anyone hurt?

36:22.681 --> 36:24.099
Cho Ye-rin, are you okay?

36:24.808 --> 36:26.267
Yes, I'm fine.

36:27.560 --> 36:28.853
You're really something.

36:28.937 --> 36:31.356
What were you thinking, going there?
Weren't you scared?

36:40.573 --> 36:41.574
Are you okay, sir?

36:43.159 --> 36:44.160
Me?

36:46.663 --> 36:47.914
SPICY MIXED RICE MASITTASHI

36:47.997 --> 36:49.207
Masittashi?

36:49.290 --> 36:50.709
What's a Masittashi?

36:52.293 --> 36:53.586
You don't know what a Masittashi is?

36:56.464 --> 36:58.466
It's our very own miracle
of the five loaves and two fish.

36:59.175 --> 37:00.760
A gift from the gods.

37:01.970 --> 37:05.098
You have acquired
a Grade B Masittashi item.

37:05.682 --> 37:08.435
When used, it provides a morale boost.

37:08.518 --> 37:10.645
During training, nothing beats this.

37:10.729 --> 37:11.813
It's the best, period.

37:12.731 --> 37:13.982
SPICY MIXED RICE MASITTASHI

37:32.542 --> 37:34.961
Now that I've added the chili oil,
how does it look?

37:35.044 --> 37:36.254
Isn't it mouth-watering?

37:37.213 --> 37:38.631
Gosh, my mouth is starting to water.

37:40.216 --> 37:42.427
- Yes, sir.
- This is the stuff.

37:44.763 --> 37:46.556
Are we really sure it's okay to eat this?

37:46.765 --> 37:48.016
It might look a little weird...

37:49.142 --> 37:50.643
but can we afford to be picky
when we're this hungry?

37:52.228 --> 37:53.229
Hey, Supplies!

37:54.689 --> 37:55.690
Damn it.

37:59.944 --> 38:00.945
Did you call for me, sir?

38:02.489 --> 38:03.490
Hey.

38:04.073 --> 38:05.492
We just came back from the dead.

38:05.950 --> 38:08.036
Do you think it makes sense
for us to eat crap

38:08.119 --> 38:09.329
because we're hungry?

38:10.205 --> 38:11.748
Don't you have anything
stashed away in the supplies?

38:13.875 --> 38:15.293
Sir, I really can't do that.

38:15.376 --> 38:16.753
Cut the crap.

38:16.836 --> 38:18.922
Meet me out back later tonight.

38:19.589 --> 38:20.632
I mean it.

38:20.715 --> 38:22.425
- Yes, sir.
- Go.

38:24.135 --> 38:25.136
Get lost.

38:56.876 --> 38:57.877
What's that?

38:59.754 --> 39:00.755
Hey, what's that?

39:01.130 --> 39:03.508
Isn't that one of those army treats?

39:09.305 --> 39:10.807
It's still warm. It must be fresh.

39:10.890 --> 39:11.891
Hey, snap out of it.

39:12.475 --> 39:14.894
If this just flew over, it means
we're getting close to enemy lines

39:14.978 --> 39:16.479
so stay on high alert. Let's move.

39:16.563 --> 39:17.856
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

39:23.486 --> 39:24.487
What is this?

39:24.696 --> 39:26.990
They said it's hard to get by
on just combat rations

39:27.073 --> 39:29.617
so the cooks tried making some rice balls.

39:29.784 --> 39:31.536
I thought it was garbage
someone threw out...

39:32.245 --> 39:33.288
Is this supposed to be food?

39:34.247 --> 39:35.665
It looks a little odd...

39:35.957 --> 39:37.625
but it's fine once you try it.

39:37.709 --> 39:39.252
Still, this looks a bit...

39:41.170 --> 39:42.338
Disgusting.

39:47.302 --> 39:49.804
Morale continues to drop.

39:51.222 --> 39:53.224
If morale drops any further...

39:53.725 --> 39:55.894
the quest will be a total failure.

39:57.228 --> 39:59.564
It doesn't matter
if it's tasty for army grunts.

39:59.647 --> 40:00.690
As long as it's fried

40:00.773 --> 40:02.442
they just go crazy and...

40:02.859 --> 40:05.028
They just stuff their faces, you know?

40:14.537 --> 40:15.622
Hero.

40:15.705 --> 40:17.332
The oil is hot enough.

40:17.582 --> 40:19.500
You may begin frying.

40:21.461 --> 40:22.545
Thanks.

40:29.552 --> 40:33.222
KOREAN RICE MILITARY BISCUITS, STAR CANDY

40:42.398 --> 40:45.777
Now this thing is just bossing
a sergeant around.

40:46.194 --> 40:47.320
Are you ready?

40:48.738 --> 40:50.073
You think this is enough?

40:50.156 --> 40:51.449
Yes, that should be plenty.

41:19.978 --> 41:22.313
- Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.
- Oh, should I do a taste test?

41:23.022 --> 41:25.233
Could you crush up the star candy, too?

41:26.734 --> 41:27.777
Jeez!

41:49.549 --> 41:52.135
SERGEANT YOON DONG-HYUN'S
RICE IN A BAG, DISGUSTING...

41:52.218 --> 41:54.178
Arancini Rice Ball.

41:54.637 --> 41:57.515
You have earned
one bonus star for creativity.

42:06.107 --> 42:08.192
Wait, is this that garbage...

42:08.276 --> 42:10.236
I mean, that same rice ball?

42:10.528 --> 42:12.447
Yes, I fried it golden brown

42:12.530 --> 42:14.240
to improve texture and appearance.

42:15.700 --> 42:17.035
Yeah, but still...

42:17.910 --> 42:19.871
I can't get what it looked like
out of my head.

42:20.121 --> 42:21.539
Is this really the time to be picky?

42:21.622 --> 42:22.999
If you don't want to eat it, don't.

42:23.082 --> 42:24.083
Master Sergeant.

42:24.584 --> 42:26.586
- I'll eat it.
- Unbelievable.

42:53.780 --> 42:55.698
EXCLUSIVE FIRST LOOK
MY FLAVOR BY THE FLAVOR BOYS

42:55.907 --> 43:00.661
MY FLAVOR BY FLAVOR BOYS, COOKING BY
KANG SEONG-JAE FEAT. YOON DONG-HYUN

43:00.828 --> 43:03.289
You must have been surprised

43:04.957 --> 43:08.461
A spark touching the tip
of your tongue for the first time

43:09.170 --> 43:11.255
The moment you take a small bite

43:11.464 --> 43:13.758
You'll get addicted to the taste

43:13.883 --> 43:16.844
A special treat made just for you

43:16.928 --> 43:19.889
You already know, don't you

43:20.139 --> 43:22.058
Behind the sweetness

43:22.141 --> 43:24.977
A special trap is hidden

43:25.061 --> 43:28.189
It'll feel unfamiliar at first

43:28.439 --> 43:30.233
But once you taste the hidden flavor

43:30.316 --> 43:31.984
Oh it's over

43:32.068 --> 43:34.612
Just taste my flavor

43:34.695 --> 43:36.864
A unique layer

43:37.031 --> 43:39.075
The moment you take a bite

43:39.158 --> 43:40.993
The sweet and sour taste spreads

43:41.077 --> 43:43.079
Baby want more?

43:43.204 --> 43:45.164
Salty or sweetie?

43:45.414 --> 43:46.958
You know it's tasty

43:47.041 --> 43:48.501
Oh tasty, right

43:48.584 --> 43:50.795
Tell me, say yes

43:54.590 --> 43:56.175
Prepare to match your taste

43:56.259 --> 43:58.344
Awakening all your senses

43:58.427 --> 44:00.429
Adding a secret just for you

44:00.513 --> 44:02.682
You'll definitely fall for it

44:02.765 --> 44:05.226
Oh, a charm different
from the first impression, like that

44:05.309 --> 44:07.353
It's not complete
without the sauce, like that

44:07.436 --> 44:11.232
A colorful savor that melts your heart

44:11.315 --> 44:14.193
The thrilling moment

44:14.277 --> 44:16.445
that sweeps through you

44:16.529 --> 44:19.240
Burnin' up, your heart's gonna blow

44:19.365 --> 44:22.243
The moment it lingers
on the tip of your lips

44:22.618 --> 44:24.412
And reaches you

44:24.620 --> 44:26.247
Oh, it's over

44:26.330 --> 44:29.000
Just taste my flavor

44:29.208 --> 44:30.918
A unique layer

44:31.294 --> 44:33.129
The moment you take a bite

44:33.462 --> 44:35.256
The sweet and sour taste spreads

44:35.339 --> 44:37.091
Baby want more?

44:37.592 --> 44:39.218
Salty or sweetie?

44:39.635 --> 44:41.220
You know it's tasty

44:41.345 --> 44:42.638
Oh tasty, right

44:42.847 --> 44:44.849
Tell me, say yes

44:44.932 --> 44:46.976
I'm sweet and juicy, baby

44:47.059 --> 44:49.061
You're so addicted, maybe

44:49.145 --> 44:50.897
Without even a moment to forget

44:50.980 --> 44:53.024
Make it wilder, make it higher

44:53.191 --> 44:55.276
And I'm so crispy, baby

44:55.359 --> 44:57.403
You're going to want me all day

44:57.486 --> 44:59.488
You'll keep coming back to me

44:59.572 --> 45:01.449
I've got your heart now

45:01.616 --> 45:03.201
Are you telling me to eat this?

45:03.326 --> 45:05.453
I'm Hwang Seok-ho.
I don't just eat anything.

45:05.536 --> 45:08.122
If I eat something like this and get sick

45:08.206 --> 45:10.374
it'll be a blow to national defense.
I'm not eating it!

45:10.499 --> 45:11.500
I don't lie, yeah.

45:11.584 --> 45:13.920
Don't hesitate, come and take it all now

45:14.003 --> 45:16.339
I'll color you entirely with me

45:16.422 --> 45:18.883
Just taste my flavor

45:19.383 --> 45:21.010
A unique layer

45:21.385 --> 45:23.387
The moment you take a bite

45:23.471 --> 45:25.348
The sweet and sour taste spreads

45:25.431 --> 45:27.308
Baby want more?

45:27.475 --> 45:29.185
Sweetie or spicy?

45:29.769 --> 45:31.354
You know it's tasty

45:31.437 --> 45:32.813
Oh tasty, right

45:32.939 --> 45:34.982
Tell me, say yes

45:35.066 --> 45:37.026
I'm sweet and juicy, baby

45:37.151 --> 45:39.111
You're so addicted, maybe

45:39.195 --> 45:40.863
Without even a moment to forget

45:40.947 --> 45:43.032
Make it wilder, make it higher

45:43.324 --> 45:45.117
And I'm so crispy, baby

45:45.451 --> 45:47.495
You're going to want me all day

45:47.578 --> 45:49.580
You'll keep coming back to me

45:49.664 --> 45:51.999
I've got your heart now

45:56.879 --> 45:57.880
So, how is it?

45:57.964 --> 45:59.465
Is it to your liking?

46:04.136 --> 46:05.388
The Company Commander...

46:07.223 --> 46:08.349
has awakened.

46:09.934 --> 46:11.686
- Sorry?
- Is it spicy?

46:11.769 --> 46:13.729
Why are you crying?

46:24.949 --> 46:27.076
I feel a sudden surge of energy.

46:30.204 --> 46:31.330
Goodness.

46:31.706 --> 46:32.999
Because we're eating during training

46:33.082 --> 46:34.458
but this is really delicious.

46:39.046 --> 46:41.549
This is crispy on the outside
and juicy on the inside.

46:42.883 --> 46:43.884
Gosh...

46:49.265 --> 46:50.683
My proud warriors.

46:50.766 --> 46:52.977
Now that we've had a hearty meal

46:53.269 --> 46:56.147
all of you will fight to the end
without giving up.

46:57.189 --> 46:58.816
- Understood?
- Yes, sir!

46:58.899 --> 46:59.984
Eat up.

47:13.748 --> 47:15.583
Mamma mia!

47:15.666 --> 47:18.085
Arancini!

47:19.378 --> 47:20.629
Don't eat it!

47:37.855 --> 47:39.357
- Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol.
- Yeah?

47:39.648 --> 47:40.649
I have some rice noodles.

47:40.733 --> 47:42.151
Would you like these?

47:42.401 --> 47:43.778
Ugh, rice noodles.

47:44.987 --> 47:46.072
Don't you have anything else?

47:47.948 --> 47:49.241
Come on, just eat these.

47:49.325 --> 47:50.493
If Yoon Dong-hyun catches me

47:50.576 --> 47:51.869
I'm seriously dead.

47:52.870 --> 47:55.122
You want me to kill you
before he does? Huh?

47:56.123 --> 47:57.333
Is this really all you have?

47:59.668 --> 48:01.670
- What are you doing?
- Damn, you scared me.

48:02.546 --> 48:04.006
Damn it.

48:04.507 --> 48:06.175
We don't have many rations left.

48:06.258 --> 48:07.843
You can't just take them like this.

48:08.094 --> 48:09.095
Hey.

48:09.178 --> 48:11.305
If there's food, we should all share.

48:12.348 --> 48:13.474
But...

48:13.557 --> 48:15.643
We'll be in big trouble
if Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun finds out.

48:17.228 --> 48:19.980
What, so Yoon Dong-hyun
is your only superior? Is that it?

48:20.064 --> 48:21.065
Hey, that's...

48:22.066 --> 48:24.402
It's not going to make a difference
if the two of us eat something.

48:24.485 --> 48:25.945
So don't worry about it and just go.

48:26.654 --> 48:29.031
But if you do this now, tomorrow...

48:29.824 --> 48:31.450
the other soldiers will really suffer.

48:32.118 --> 48:34.245
This little punk...

48:35.287 --> 48:37.248
You act like you care about soldiers

48:37.331 --> 48:39.166
but you caused the food poisoning.

48:39.250 --> 48:41.043
Can't you see everyone's
practically dying because of you?

48:48.467 --> 48:51.804
Wow, look at the glare on this punk.
And he just got here.

48:54.557 --> 48:55.599
Follow me.

48:57.643 --> 48:58.811
Damn it.

49:01.897 --> 49:03.149
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol.

49:14.285 --> 49:15.661
- You little...
- I'm...

49:20.291 --> 49:22.418
Activating the Chef's Eye.

49:23.878 --> 49:25.713
- Damn it.
- "Damn it"?

49:27.047 --> 49:28.841
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol,
that's not what I meant.

49:29.675 --> 49:31.469
You're really getting out of line.

49:31.760 --> 49:33.721
SERGEANT YOON DONG-HYUN'S RICE IN A BAG

49:33.804 --> 49:36.849
When someone's talking, you should
at least look at them. Damn.

49:38.601 --> 49:40.227
I think there's someone under the ground.

49:46.275 --> 49:48.986
He's really putting on a show.
That crazy bastard.

49:53.991 --> 49:56.785
Hey, did you see that crazy bastard?
He's openly acting insane now.

49:56.869 --> 49:58.370
But what if he's really seeing something?

49:59.622 --> 50:01.165
There's a rumor
when he stares off like that

50:01.248 --> 50:03.125
he's seeing dead soldiers.

50:03.209 --> 50:05.544
Oh, give me a break.

50:05.878 --> 50:08.631
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol,
what if he goes and snitches?

50:08.714 --> 50:10.299
You should get going, quickly.

50:10.841 --> 50:11.842
Yeah.

50:12.468 --> 50:13.552
Hey, wait up, you idiot.

50:19.767 --> 50:22.645
- Salute!
- Kang Seong-jae. What is it?

50:22.937 --> 50:25.397
Ma'am, there's something you need to see.

50:41.121 --> 50:42.623
- This way?
- Yes.

50:42.706 --> 50:44.542
I found tracks around here.

50:44.625 --> 50:46.502
Are you sure you weren't just
seeing things from lack of sleep?

50:46.585 --> 50:47.586
Quiet.

50:49.171 --> 50:50.172
This way.

50:50.506 --> 50:52.132
- Move out.
- Moving out.

51:18.409 --> 51:20.452
Tunnel discovered. Moving in.

51:55.904 --> 51:57.948
SERGEANT YOON DONG-HYUN'S RICE IN A BAG

52:09.710 --> 52:13.339
The soldiers' morale has reached 80%.

52:13.631 --> 52:14.715
COMBAT STATS INCREASED

52:14.798 --> 52:17.509
Your Combat Stats are increasing.

52:37.488 --> 52:40.824
Killed.

52:50.626 --> 52:52.961
I felt like I could hit my targets
with my eyes closed today.

52:53.045 --> 52:55.172
It was like I was dancing with my rifle.

52:56.799 --> 52:57.800
Yeah!

53:03.555 --> 53:06.350
Company Commander,
the opposing force has been wiped out.

53:06.767 --> 53:08.519
- Yeah!
- Okay! That's it!

53:10.312 --> 53:13.315
We did it! We did it!

53:21.990 --> 53:24.284
How did he find the opposing force
hidden in that tunnel...

53:24.368 --> 53:26.453
I really didn't think
he'd actually find them.

53:26.829 --> 53:28.330
I know, right?

53:28.414 --> 53:29.873
What the hell is he?

53:32.418 --> 53:33.961
I should've joined the special forces.

53:34.253 --> 53:35.254
The special forces.

53:38.590 --> 53:40.050
- Yoon Dong-hyun.
- Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

53:40.134 --> 53:41.343
Have you seen Kang Seong-jae?

53:42.010 --> 53:43.554
Weren't you two together?

53:59.778 --> 54:00.946
It's so dark...

54:01.405 --> 54:03.574
I can't tell where I am.

54:19.381 --> 54:20.424
What's this?

54:21.091 --> 54:22.551
Is everyone out on a mission?

54:22.801 --> 54:23.802
Yes.

54:24.052 --> 54:25.345
From what I've confirmed

54:25.637 --> 54:27.222
they don't seem to have noticed yet.

54:30.768 --> 54:32.770
There's no one left to cause trouble

54:33.228 --> 54:36.064
so you should be able to
finish this deal quietly.

54:39.443 --> 54:40.819
You mean Cho Ye-rin, right?

54:44.448 --> 54:46.325
We sent her away to the Outpost.

54:46.408 --> 54:47.785
What's she going to do?

54:49.077 --> 54:50.078
Well...

54:50.370 --> 54:51.663
If you're really worried...

54:56.293 --> 54:57.669
should I just take care of her?

55:55.227 --> 55:56.478
Who the hell was that?

55:56.812 --> 55:58.021
Show yourself!

57:21.396 --> 57:23.857
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

57:24.274 --> 57:25.442
Kang Seong-jae!

57:25.525 --> 57:27.444
We've received a report of a problem.

57:28.695 --> 57:30.572
The whole unit is about to be screwed.

57:30.822 --> 57:33.408
- Our great war hero.
- Private Kang Seong-jae!

57:33.784 --> 57:35.369
We can't just let this be.

57:35.535 --> 57:37.329
You're finally going on that leave
you wouldn't shut up about.

57:37.496 --> 57:39.623
This is great. But Kwan-cheol, that jerk.

57:39.706 --> 57:42.584
Turn the soldier who dislikes you the most

57:42.668 --> 57:45.003
- into an ally.
- Come here.

57:46.004 --> 57:48.298
If I'm not around,
he thinks he owns the place.

57:49.675 --> 57:51.301
Hey, I'm just curious.

57:51.385 --> 57:53.011
Kang Seong-jae!

57:53.095 --> 57:54.554
You think you own the place, don't you?
